==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[syneresis]] {{qualifier|US}}, [[synæresis]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc}} {{term|συναίρεσις||unification|sc=polytonic|tr=sunairesis|lang=grc}} < {{term|συν||together|sc=polytonic|tr=sun|lang=grc}} + {{term|αἵρεσις||taking|sc=polytonic|tr=airesis|lang=grc}} < {{term|αἱρέω||I take|sc=polytonic|tr=aireō|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}
{{examples-right|sense=linguistics, prosody|examples=contraction of the ''-ew'' ({{IPA|/uː/}}) and ''or-'' ({{IPA|/oʊɹ/}}) of ''[[w:New Orleans|New Orleans]]'' into {{IPA|/'''nɔː'''lənz/}}.}}
# {{linguistics|prosody}} the [[contraction]] of two [[vowel]]s into a [[diphthong]] or a [[long vowel]].
# {{chemistry}} the [[separating]] out of the [[liquid]] from a [[gel]].

